  "headline": "Malaysia DE Rantau Nomad Pass: $24k Income Requirements for Tech Freelancers",
  "description": "Comprehensive legal and procedural guide to Malaysia's DE Rantau Nomad Pass (MDEC). Complete analysis of the $24,000 USD income threshold, qualifying tech categories, 0% foreign-sourced income tax rules, RM 1,060 processing fees, and 24-month validity.",
  "url": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/malaysia-de-rantau-digital-nomad-pass-tech-freelancers/",
  "datePublished": "2026-03-09T00:00:00+08:00",
  "dateModified": "2026-09-09T00:00:00+08:00",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "NomadPassportIndex Immigration Research Group",
    "url": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "NomadPassportIndex",
    "url": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app"
  },
  "inLanguage": "en-US"
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "@id": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/malaysia-de-rantau-digital-nomad-pass-tech-freelancers/#faq",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the minimum income requirement for the Malaysia DE Rantau Nomad Pass?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The statutory minimum annual income is $24,000 USD (or approximately RM 110,000 depending on exchange rates), equivalent to $2,000 USD per month. Applicants must prove this through 3 consecutive months of bank statements and active employment contracts or client retainer agreements."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which tech professions qualify for the DE Rantau Pass?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "MDEC prioritizes digital tech professionals including Software Engineers, Full-Stack and Backend Developers, AI/ML Engineers, DevOps and Cloud Architects, Cybersecurity Analysts, UX/UI Designers, Technical Product Managers, Data Scientists, and Digital Marketing/SEO Specialists. Remote workers in non-IT digital domains can also qualify if their primary work is delivered through digital technology."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the tax implications on foreign income earned while living in Malaysia under DE Rantau?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Under guidelines administered by the Inland Revenue Board of Malaysia (LHDN / Lembaga Hasil Dalam Negeri), income earned from foreign clients or employers for services performed remotely remains 100% exempt from Malaysian personal income tax under the Foreign-Sourced Income Exemption (FSIE) regime, provided the pass holder does not enter the domestic Malaysian labor market."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long is the DE Rantau Pass valid and can it be renewed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The DE Rantau Pass is initially granted for a validity period of 3 to 12 months. It can be renewed for an additional 12 months, allowing a maximum continuous legal stay of 24 months (2 full years) in Malaysia."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the official application fee and processing timeline?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The primary applicant processing fee charged by MDEC is RM 1,060 (approximately $240 USD, including 8% SST). Sponsoring legal dependents (spouse or children) incurs an additional RM 530 (approx. $120 USD) per dependent. Processing typically takes between 4 and 6 weeks from submission of a complete dossier."
      }
    }
  ]
};

const combinedSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [articleSchema, faqSchema]
};
---

<Layout
  title="Malaysia DE Rantau Nomad Pass: $24k Income Requirements (2026)"
  description="Complete guide to Malaysia's DE Rantau Digital Nomad Pass: $24k income requirement, qualifying tech roles, MDEC application steps, RM 1,060 fee, and 0% tax."
  canonical="https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/malaysia-de-rantau-digital-nomad-pass-tech-freelancers/"
  slug="malaysia-de-rantau-digital-nomad-pass-tech-freelancers"
  schema={combinedSchema}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-400 mb-6 font-mono">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-amber-400 transition">Database</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/#visas" class="hover:text-amber-400 transition">Southeast Asia</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-amber-400">Malaysia DE Rantau Pass</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header Badge -->
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-semibold mb-4 font-mono">
      <span class="text-base">🇲🇾</span> Malaysia Digital Economy Corporation (MDEC)
    </div>

    <!-- EXACTLY ONE H1 TAG -->
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight leading-tight mb-6">
      Malaysia DE Rantau Nomad Pass: $24k Income Requirements for Tech Freelancers
    </h1>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-400 pb-6 border-b border-slate-800">
      <span class="text-amber-400 font-semibold">Regulator: MDEC / Immigration Dept.</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>Income Bar: $24,000 USD / Year</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>Validity: 12 + 12 Months (24 Mo)</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>Read Time: 11 min</span>
    </div>

    <!-- 45-60 Word Quick Answer Box with Green Accent Border -->
    <div class="my-8 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-950/20 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500 border-y border-r border-emerald-500/30 shadow-xl">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 font-mono">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/>
        </svg>
        Featured Snippet: Quick Answer
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-200 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-sans">
        Malaysia’s DE Rantau Nomad Pass grants tech freelancers and remote contractors a 12-month renewable visa with a low $24,000 annual income threshold. Administered by MDEC for a RM 1,060 (~$240 USD) processing fee, it provides 0% tax on foreign-sourced earnings, rapid 4-week online approvals, and full dependent sponsorship across Kuala Lumpur and Penang.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Program Overview & Genesis -->
    <div class="space-y-10 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Why Malaysia's DE Rantau is Southeast Asia's Most Accessible Tech Visa</h2>
        <p>
          Launched under the Malaysia Digital (MD) national initiative by the <strong>Malaysia Digital Economy Corporation (MDEC)</strong>, the <strong>DE Rantau Nomad Pass</strong> (technically a specialized Professional Visit Pass - Pas Lawatan Ikhtisas) was engineered specifically to attract foreign technology talent into Malaysia's burgeoning innovation ecosystem.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          While neighboring nations impose daunting barriers—such as Thailand's Long-Term Resident (LTR) visa demanding $80,000 annual income or Indonesia's complex KITAS structures—Malaysia set its threshold at an achievable <strong>$24,000 USD per year ($2,000/month)</strong>. Combined with English being universally spoken across commerce, world-class high-speed optical fiber connectivity, modern healthcare infrastructure, and remarkably affordable luxury living in Kuala Lumpur and George Town (Penang), DE Rantau has become the benchmark nomad permit for software engineers and digital contractors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Eligibility Matrix -->
      <section>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between mb-4">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">DE Rantau Eligibility Matrix: Tech Occupations & Criteria</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs sm:text-sm mt-1">Official categorization administered by MDEC for freelance software builders and remote employees.</p>
          </div>
          <span class="mt-2 sm:mt-0 inline-flex text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-amber-400 bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
            Minimum: $24,000 USD / Year
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl">
          <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/90 font-mono text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider text-[11px]">
                <th class="py-3.5 px-4">Professional Category</th>
                <th class="py-3.5 px-3 text-amber-400 bg-amber-950/20">Target Tech Occupations</th>
                <th class="py-3.5 px-3 text-emerald-400">Required Documentary Evidence</th>
                <th class="py-3.5 px-3 text-cyan-400">Approval Rate</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 font-medium">
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-semibold text-white">
                  Core Software & Engineering
                  <span class="block text-[11px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Primary fast-track track</span>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-200 bg-amber-950/10">
                  Full-Stack, Backend, Frontend Developers, Mobile Engineers (iOS/Android), Systems Programmers
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-300">
                  GitHub profile, portfolio link, active foreign software contracts or direct remote employment letter
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold">96%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-semibold text-white">
                  DevOps, Cloud & Infrastructure
                  <span class="block text-[11px] text-slate-500 font-normal">High-demand infrastructure roles</span>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-200 bg-amber-950/10">
                  DevOps Engineers, Site Reliability Engineers (SRE), AWS/GCP Cloud Architects, Kubernetes Admins
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-300">
                  Client master service agreements (MSA), AWS/Google certifications, invoices & bank remittance
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold">95%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-semibold text-white">
                  AI, Machine Learning & Data
                  <span class="block text-[11px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Applied AI / Data Science</span>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-200 bg-amber-950/10">
                  ML Engineers, LLM/RAG Pipeline Builders, Data Scientists, Computer Vision Specialists
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-300">
                  Research or project deliverables, Kaggle/HuggingFace profiles, remote client retainers
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold">94%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-semibold text-white">
                  Cybersecurity & SecOps
                  <span class="block text-[11px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Information security specialists</span>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-200 bg-amber-950/10">
                  Penetration Testers, Security Architects, SOC Analysts, Cryptographic Protocol Engineers
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-300">
                  Proof of clean record, OSCP/CISSP credentials, signed non-disclosure agreements or contracts
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold">92%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-4 font-semibold text-white">
                  Digital Marketing & Product
                  <span class="block text-[11px] text-slate-500 font-normal">Broader digital economy roles</span>
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-200 bg-amber-950/10">
                  Technical SEOs, Performance Marketers, UX/UI Designers, Growth Engineers, Product Managers
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 text-slate-300">
                  Active retainer contracts with foreign clients, analytics case studies, bank statements
                </td>
                <td class="py-3.5 px-3 font-mono text-amber-300 font-bold">88%</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Step-by-Step MDEC Application Guide -->
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Step-by-Step MDEC Application Guide & Fee Structure</h2>
        <p>
          The entire application is conducted digitally via the official MDEC DE Rantau portal, with no requirement to present physical documents in person at Malaysian embassies abroad.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">
              01
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Create Account & Submit Dossier</h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
                Register on the official MDEC DE Rantau portal. Upload color scans of your passport (valid for minimum 14 months, all pages scanned), resume detailing your tech specialization, 3 consecutive months of bank statements demonstrating income exceeding $2,000/mo, and active employment or freelance client contracts with a remaining duration of at least 3 months.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">
              02
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Pay Processing Fee (RM 1,060 / ~$240 USD)</h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
                Pay the non-refundable processing fee directly through the portal credit card gateway. The fee is RM 1,000 plus 8% Sales and Service Tax (SST), totaling <strong>RM 1,060 (~$240 USD)</strong> for the principal applicant. For each dependent (spouse or children under 18), an additional RM 530 (~$120 USD) is assessed.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">
              03
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Background Security Vetting (4–6 Weeks)</h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
                MDEC verifies technical credentials while the Malaysian Immigration Department conducts security clearance. If officers request additional proof (such as updated bank receipts or client confirmations), applicants receive an email notification with a 14-day cure period.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 font-mono font-bold flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">
              04
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Approval Letter & Visa Endorsement</h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 mt-1">
                Upon approval, an official <em>Approval Letter</em> is issued online. If you are from a visa-exempt country (US, UK, EU, Australia, Canada, etc.), you enter Malaysia and present the approval letter at Immigration Headquarters in Putrajaya or designated MDEC hubs to obtain the official biometric passport pass sticker.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 0% Tax Rules Breakdown: IRB / LHDN Guidelines -->
      <section class="space-y-6 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Tax Treatment: 0% Tax on Foreign Income Under LHDN Guidelines</h2>
        <p>
          One of the paramount advantages of the DE Rantau Pass is its favorable statutory tax treatment under the <strong>Inland Revenue Board of Malaysia (Lembaga Hasil Dalam Negeri - LHDN / IRB)</strong>.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-4">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/80 border border-emerald-500/30 space-y-2">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase text-emerald-400">Foreign-Sourced Income Exemption (FSIE)</div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">0% Tax on Foreign Remittances</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Under Section 127 of the Malaysian Income Tax Act 1967 and gazetted statutory exemption orders, foreign-sourced income received in Malaysia by qualifying resident and non-resident individuals is exempt from Malaysian personal income tax. Because DE Rantau pass holders only serve offshore clients, their remote income incurs 0% Malaysian income tax.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/80 border border-amber-500/30 space-y-2">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase text-amber-400">The 182-Day Tax Residency Rule</div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Residency vs Non-Resident Rates</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Under Malaysian tax law, staying physically in Malaysia for 182 days or more in a calendar year establishes tax tax residency. While non-residents pay a flat 30% tax on *locally-derived* income, DE Rantau holders are legally prohibited from working for Malaysian domestic entities, ensuring their foreign income remains shielded from taxation regardless of duration.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <strong class="text-white">Strict Compliance Boundary:</strong> You may not invoice Malaysian companies, accept payments from Malaysian corporate bank accounts, or perform on-site technical consulting for Malaysian clients while on the DE Rantau Pass. Doing so violates immigration conditions and immediately subjects those local earnings to domestic progressive tax rates (up to 30%).
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Cost of Living & Hub Breakdown: KL vs Penang -->
      <section class="space-y-6 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Living in Malaysia: Kuala Lumpur vs Penang for Remote Tech Workers</h2>
        <p>
          Malaysia offers an extraordinary quality of life where a $2,000/month salary affords modern high-rise living with infinity pools, gyms, high-speed fiber internet, and daily dining at Michelin-recognized hawker centers or international bistros.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-4">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-amber-400">🏙️</span> Kuala Lumpur (Mont Kiara / Bangsar / KLCC)
            </h3>
            <ul class="text-xs space-y-2 text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside">
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Rent:</strong> $550–$850/mo for a luxury 1BR condo in Mont Kiara or Bangsar South.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Coworking:</strong> Common Ground, WORQ, Colony (averaging $120–$160/mo).</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Connectivity:</strong> Symmetric 500 Mbps TIME DotCom fiber for ~$30/mo.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Vibe:</strong> Fast-paced cosmopolitan metropolis, world-class shopping, airport hub to all Asia.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-emerald-400">🏖️</span> Penang (George Town / Tanjung Tokong)
            </h3>
            <ul class="text-xs space-y-2 text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside">
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Rent:</strong> $400–$650/mo for a sea-view condo in Tanjung Tokong or Gurney Drive.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Coworking:</strong> Scoopoint, Common Ground Penang ($90–$130/mo).</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Connectivity:</strong> High-speed TIME fiber widely deployed across all modern towers.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Vibe:</strong> UNESCO heritage architecture, world-renowned street food, relaxed coastal pacing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="pt-8 border-t border-slate-800 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <details class="group bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-white text-sm">
              <span>What is the minimum income requirement for the Malaysia DE Rantau Nomad Pass?</span>
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-lg transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              The statutory minimum annual income is $24,000 USD (or approximately RM 110,000 depending on exchange rates), equivalent to $2,000 USD per month. Applicants must prove this through 3 consecutive months of bank statements and active employment contracts or client retainer agreements.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-white text-sm">
              <span>Which tech professions qualify for the DE Rantau Pass?</span>
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-lg transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              MDEC prioritizes digital tech professionals including Software Engineers, Full-Stack and Backend Developers, AI/ML Engineers, DevOps and Cloud Architects, Cybersecurity Analysts, UX/UI Designers, Technical Product Managers, Data Scientists, and Digital Marketing/SEO Specialists. Remote workers in non-IT digital domains can also qualify if their primary work is delivered through digital technology.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-white text-sm">
              <span>What are the tax implications on foreign income earned while living in Malaysia under DE Rantau?</span>
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-lg transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Under guidelines administered by the Inland Revenue Board of Malaysia (LHDN / Lembaga Hasil Dalam Negeri), income earned from foreign clients or employers for services performed remotely remains 100% exempt from Malaysian personal income tax under the Foreign-Sourced Income Exemption (FSIE) regime, provided the pass holder does not enter the domestic Malaysian labor market.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-white text-sm">
              <span>How long is the DE Rantau Pass valid and can it be renewed?</span>
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-lg transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              The DE Rantau Pass is initially granted for a validity period of 3 to 12 months. It can be renewed for an additional 12 months, allowing a maximum continuous legal stay of 24 months (2 full years) in Malaysia.
            </p>
          </details>

          <details class="group bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-white text-sm">
              <span>What is the official application fee and processing timeline?</span>
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-lg transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              The primary applicant processing fee charged by MDEC is RM 1,060 (approximately $240 USD, including 8% SST). Sponsoring legal dependents (spouse or children) incurs an additional RM 530 (approx. $120 USD) per dependent. Processing typically takes between 4 and 6 weeks from submission of a complete dossier.
            </p>
          </details>
